==Enemy==
Winged Pigge has a very fast attack rate and 100% chance to [[Weaken]] cats to 10% for 5 seconds, which can gravely cripple whatever attackers you're using against her. If that wasn't bad enough, she also has decent movement speed, high health and DPS, and Omni Strike reaching up to 340 range. Her standing range is relatively low at only 170, but it ends up working in her favor: combined with her high DPS and Omni Strike piercing, it allows her to tear through defenses and render your non-[[:Category:Cats with Weaken Immunity|Weaken-immune]] attackers entirely ineffective.

Although she may not seem that deadly on her own, Winged Pigge often forms a synergy with extreme threats such as [[R.Ost]] in [[Heaven's Oasis]], [[Super Metal Hippoe]] in [[Woods of Resentment]], and [[Commander Ostromeda]] in [[Creamy Snowplain]], where the main answers to the aformentioned enemies do not fare well against Winged Pigge.

==Strategy==
Do not let Winged Pigge weaken your attackers, as that will make her extremely difficult to get rid of. Because she has long reach and piercing attacks, tanky meatshields such as [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] and/or [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] are best against her.
*[[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] outranges her, deals heavy damage when stacked, and being Immune to Weaken, she will not be crippled as much if Winged Pigge does hit. Beware her high cost, however, as she can drain your funds and ultimately cost you a victory. She may not be as effective later on, especially in Uncanny Legends where she is often too cost-inefficient to provide any real value. Instead, you can simply use [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] and get better value for their better cost-efficiency, despite their lack of Weaken Immunity.
*[[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]] is a useful tank against Winged Pigge; and should be unlocked at this point in the game. If not already, hypermax this cat without regret.
*[[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Miasma Cat]] outranges her, is cheap, spammable, deals Massive Damage and is Immune to Weaken, so he can take out huge chunks of her health when stacked, especially in [[True Form]]. Keep this cat safe with Ramen Cat, spam them, and watch as this Angelic fiend is destroyed. Due to his cheap cost, you can pair him up with almost any other attacker of your choice, but always bring Ramen Cat along to ensure that Winged Pigge won't stand a chance to push. Keep in mind that Miasma Cat is extremely fragile, and likely won't survive more than two attacks from Winged Pigges at higher magnifications.
*Many Uber Rares from the [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|ULTRA SOULS]] set are excellent counters to this enemy: [[Urashima Taro (Uber Rare Cat)|King Gamereon]] for his resistance to Angels and Immunity to Weaken, being able to nearly solo her at level 40; [[Momotaro (Uber Rare Cat)|The Peach Devils]] for their ability to freeze her, and if [[Talents|Talented]], weaken her too; [[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Jizo's Moving/Mega-Castle]] for its huge damage, being able to kill her in a few hits, although if you are using his True Form, be mindful of other attackers that may do enough damage to cause Winged Pigge to be knocked back by the first two multi-hit attacks; and [[Kintaro (Uber Rare Cat)|Kinrangers Robo/GigaForce]] for being able to slow her, and in True Form, Curse her to disable her weaken ability.
*[[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kalisa]] will be weakened and knocked back before she can hit Winged Pigge, so her first strike is the most valuable against her (she only outranges Winged Pigge's Omni Strike by 15). Otherwise, it is recommended to use [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]], as he deals extreme damage and is immune to weaken; and can effectively do what Kalisa should do. However, Winged Pigge typically inflicts too much damage for Greater Balrog Demon Cat to get a clean hit off unless support and [[Talents]] are put into the equation.
*[[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli the Bane]] is excellent against Winged Pigge, as she outranges Winged Pigge's Omni Strike by 60 and can consistently curse her, making her primary gimmick useless. Even if Winged Pigge does hit, Kasli the Bane's immunity to Weaken won't make her get crippled down.
*[[Mighty Rekon Korps (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Rekon Korps]] works well against Winged Pigge, as it can be expected to be knocked back, then start an attack that will hit just after the weaken effect runs out, thus making Winged Pigge's weaken ability basically ineffective.
*[[Goddess of Light Sirius (Uber Rare Cat)|Goddess of Light Sirius]] is an amazing choice of a unit, as she outranges Winged Pigge's Omni Strikes, is immune to weaken, and can tank a few hits seeing as Sirius has Strong Against and is decently tanky already.

Once you have [[Ancient Egg: N110 (Rare Cat)|Farmboy Cat]] and/or [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Master of Mind Catcrates]], these two units can easily paralyze Winged Pigge to where you don't need any meatshields; she only reaches far with her Omni Strike, but her standing range is low. By setting up Winged Pigge to be slowed by a stack of Farmboy Cats and optionally (but very recommended) followed up by Catcrates, you can use units like [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]], [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]] and the like to easily kill her when your attackers stack up. Just make sure to clear out any peon that may get in the way of Farmboy Cat and don't meatshield because it'll trigger Winged Pigge's piercing attacks.

